comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-16T22:25:26.735Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-08-17: searched all statuses for linked test output buffer, max_buffer, stdout write, UNKNOWN write, EAGAIN, verbose child, and coverage capture. Closed pm-j36ypd and pm-5sm91o own two previously shipped EAGAIN fixes; their own lineage treats a released-version recurrence with contradictory evidence as a distinct child issue. Open pm-e97jyf covers schema-context divergence, not output transport. This item records the new UNKNOWN SyncWriteStream recurrence without reopening completed historical fixes."
  "2026-08-17T02:03:48.256Z","harness:codex","Start evidence 2026-08-17: Auto Release run 31985913468 passed build, exact coverage, packed npx smoke, and 88-command package-first dogfood, then correctly stopped before tag creation on Sentry PM-CLI-36. Live event 2e031518369e4998abae876a2035cae9 is a single handled pm-cli@2026.8.16 Node 26/Arch copyfile errno -122 during linked-test tracker seeding. Host diagnostics show /tmp at 98% inode use while runLinkedTests eagerly initializes four trackers and copies tracker data even for the selected non-PM coverage command. Active fix will make tracker sandbox data demand-driven and prove non-tracker runs avoid the high-inode copy path."
  "2026-08-17T02:29:54.275Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: the first PM-linked coverage run under /tmp at 98% inode use completed all 511 files and 7,457 tests without the prior copyfile EDQUOT failure; the strict gate then correctly found one uncovered defensive null branch. After adding the negative control, pm test pm-giks4s --run --only-index 2 passed in the same schema sandbox with source_project_item_count=2512 and sandbox_project_item_count=0. Exact coverage is 54,508/54,508 statements, 40,594/40,594 branches, 11,205/11,205 functions, and 52,609/52,609 lines. Repo-wide pnpm lint passed ESLint, zero jscpd clones, static assurance, package boundaries, SDK parity, graph composition, and record integrity. Secret scan, production dependency audit, package artifact gate, docs link gate, latest pm-changelog 2026.8.16 install/check, and a fresh temporary packed-package npx plus bunx version/contracts smoke all passed."
  "2026-08-17T02:41:12.761Z","harness:codex","Hosted exact-head CI run 31988312977 exposed the defect-evidence contract omitted at closure: escape_class and structured gate_evidence were missing. Added production_defect classification plus the linked-test-demand-driven-sandbox gate receipt with local and hosted checks and a runnable negative control. pnpm quality:defect-evidence now passes with findings=0; this is a PM metadata governance correction, not a code bypass."
  "2026-08-17T02:42:08.587Z","harness:codex","Review feedback accepted: moved destination mkdir into the same typed seed_linked_test host boundary as copy, corrected docs to describe effective schema context rather than all non-PM commands, and changed the canonical title so generated changelog language states the user-visible capability. Operational diagnosis remains in immutable PM history."
  "2026-08-17T02:46:05.963Z","harness:codex","Additional CodeRabbit negative-control request accepted: the test seam now forces numeric EDQUOT specifically from destination-directory creation and proves the error exits as host_environment_capacity_fault with reason EDQUOT. Focused verification passes 74 tests, plus ESLint and full TypeScript project/typetest checks."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-17T02:29:53.761Z","harness:codex","Demand-driven context materialization is both a correctness and resource-safety primitive: decide effective linked-command context before sandbox initialization, and never copy tracker data for schema or non-PM runs."
